---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';

const title = 'Projected Results and the Math | Exhibit Automation';
const description =
  "We are new, so instead of case studies we publish the math: what missed calls cost, what we expect to recover, and every source behind it.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/results">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Results</span>
      <h1>We are new. Here is the math instead of case studies.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Every agency site you visit has testimonials. Ours does not yet, because we have not earned them. What we can
        show you is exactly how we expect to make you money, using published industry benchmarks, with the assumptions
        written out so you can argue with them.
      </p>
      <div class="card promise">
        <p><b>The promise on this page:</b> no invented client quotes, no borrowed logos, no numbers without a source. When we have three clients with ninety days of data, this page becomes real case studies and this note goes away.</p>
        <p class="small">We re-verify every figure on this site periodically. In our first September 2026 pass we removed two claims we could not trace to any primary research and corrected four others against better sources. A second pass later that month replaced several home services, law and auto repair figures whose cited pages did not actually contain them, and changed the projections below to match. Where a number comes from a company selling something, we say so next to it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Property management · 200 units, 2 properties</span>
      <h2>Recovered leases and returned hours.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>The assumptions</h3>
          <ul class="checks">
            <li>30 leasing inquiries a month</li>
            <li>60% currently unanswered or answered too late, so 18 lost<sup><a href="#fn1">1</a></sup></li>
            <li>We recover 12 of the 18</li>
            <li>25% lead-to-lease conversion</li>
            <li>Each recovered lease is worth one month's rent, $1,500</li>
            <li>40% annual turnover, so 80 turns a year, each five days shorter, worth $225 to $375<sup><a href="#fn2">2</a></sup></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>The arithmetic</h3>
          <p>12 recovered × 25% = <b>3 additional leases a month</b>. At $1,500 each that is $27,000 a year if it only happens in a six-month leasing season, and $54,000 if it holds all year.</p>
          <p>Faster turns: 80 × $225 to $375 = $18,000 to $30,000 a year. The two overlap slightly, so the top of the range is optimistic.</p>
          <p>Staff time: Buildium reports up to 12 hours a week saved per 20 units on communication and admin.<sup><a href="#fn3">3</a></sup> At 200 units we project conservatively 20+ hours a week.</p>
          <p class="small">A 30-minute delay in responding drops renter engagement from 40% to 10%, so speed is doing most of the work here.<sup><a href="#fn4">4</a></sup></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card total">
        <div class="stat"><b>$45K to $84K</b><span>projected annual recovered rent and avoided vacancy</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b>800+ hrs</b><span>projected staff hours returned per year</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b>$12,000</b><span>Managed Agent cost per year at this size</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Home services · 2-truck HVAC shop</span>
      <h2>The jobs that went to whoever answered.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>The assumptions</h3>
          <ul class="checks">
            <li>60 inbound calls in a busy week</li>
            <li>40% missed, so 24 unanswered. The benchmark is worse: 48% of home-services callers never reach a person<sup><a href="#fn5">5</a></sup></li>
            <li>65% of those would have booked, so about 16 jobs<sup><a href="#fn6">6</a></sup></li>
            <li>We recover half to two thirds, 8 to 10 a week</li>
            <li>$450 average revenue per booked job, the bottom of the published range<sup><a href="#fn6">6</a></sup></li>
            <li>26 to 40 weeks a year at this volume, because HVAC is seasonal</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>The arithmetic</h3>
          <p>8 to 10 recovered jobs × $450 = <b>$3,600 to $4,500 a week</b>.</p>
          <p>26 weeks × $3,600 = $93,600. 40 weeks × $4,500 = $180,000.</p>
          <p>Recovery rate is the assumption we are least sure of. Vendor-reported improvements in this category are large but we have found no independent study, so treat the 8 to 10 figure as our estimate, not a benchmark.<sup><a href="#fn7">7</a></sup></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card total">
        <div class="stat"><b>$94K to $180K</b><span>projected annual recovered job revenue</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b>Under 60 sec</b><span>target first response, any hour</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b>$15,000</b><span>Managed Agent cost per year at 2 to 3 trucks</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Law firms · 3 attorneys</span>
      <h2>The callers who did not leave a voicemail.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>The assumptions</h3>
          <ul class="checks">
            <li>40 inquiries a month</li>
            <li>Clio's secret-shopper study found only 40% of firms answered the phone at all<sup><a href="#fn8">8</a></sup></li>
            <li>We model a more conservative 35% miss rate, so 14 unanswered<sup><a href="#fn9">9</a></sup></li>
            <li>Some of those call back on their own. We recover 5 to 7</li>
            <li>30% consult-to-retain, $3,000 average matter</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>The arithmetic</h3>
          <p>5 to 7 recovered × 30% × $3,000 = <b>$4,500 to $6,300 a month</b>, or $54,000 to $75,600 a year.</p>
          <p>Clio has also found that firms which improve client onboarding, including online intake tools, average 50% more potential clients and 50% more revenue.<sup><a href="#fn8">8</a></sup></p>
          <p class="small">Only 42% of consumers say they leave a voicemail when a business does not answer.<sup><a href="#fn10">10</a></sup></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card total">
        <div class="stat"><b>$54K to $76K</b><span>projected annual additional retained matters</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b>Under 60 sec</b><span>target first response to a new inquiry</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b>$15,000</b><span>Managed Agent cost per year at 3 to 5 attorneys</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Where this could be wrong</span>
      <h2>The assumptions most likely to break.</h2>
      <ul class="checks waits">
        <li><b>Your missed-call rate may be lower than the benchmark.</b> If you already answer 90% of calls, the recovery number shrinks a lot. We measure yours during the build rather than assuming.</li>
        <li><b>Recovered does not mean closed.</b> We answer faster and capture more; your team still has to run the tour or the consult well.</li>
        <li><b>Seasonality is real.</b> Three extra leases a month is a leasing-season number, not a February number. HVAC swings the same way.</li>
        <li><b>Average values are averages.</b> A $450 ticket and a $3,000 matter may not be yours. The calculators on each industry page let you use your own numbers.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="small">If we cannot make the arithmetic work with your real numbers on the intro call, we will say so and not take the project.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA title="Run the math on your own numbers." body="The calculator on each industry page uses your call volume, your close rate and your ticket size. If the result is not a multiple of what we cost, do not hire us." />

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="footnote" id="fn1">1. 60.8% of calls to multifamily properties went unanswered in an analysis of 170,825 calls in one quarter, presented by Fiona at Cadence Connect and reported by <a href="https://digible.com/our-thoughts/why-missed-calls-are-costing-you-leases-data-driven-insights-and-solutions-for-multifamily-operators/" rel="nofollow noopener">Digible</a>.</p>
      <p class="footnote" id="fn2">2. Avoided vacancy value per turn and median list-to-lease: <a href="https://www.onewave-ai.com/blog/ai-for-property-management-smb-playbook" rel="nofollow noopener">OneWave AI, 2026</a>. The 40% turnover rate is our assumption.</p>
      <p class="footnote" id="fn3">3. Hours saved per 20-unit portfolio: <a href="https://www.buildium.com/blog/best-ai-property-management-tools/" rel="nofollow noopener">Buildium, 2026</a>. This is Buildium's claim about its own AI tooling, not an independent benchmark.</p>
      <p class="footnote" id="fn4">4. <a href="https://use.rently.com/blog/rently-2026-renter-touring-expectations-report/" rel="nofollow noopener">Rently 2026 Renter Touring Expectations Report</a>, an online survey of 800 US renters conducted in May 2026 via Pollfish.</p>
      <p class="footnote" id="fn5">5. <a href="https://www.invoca.com/reports/the-invoca-home-services-lead-conversion-benchmarks-report-2026" rel="nofollow noopener">Invoca Home Services Lead Conversion Benchmarks Report, 2026</a>: 52% of callers to home-service businesses speak with a person, across more than 70 million tracked calls. Invoca sells call-tracking software.</p>
      <p class="footnote" id="fn6">6. Service Roundtable benchmarks for residential HVAC ($450 to $950 average revenue per booked call, 65% booking rate), as reported by <a href="https://ainora.lt/blog/hvac-service-call-statistics-2026" rel="nofollow noopener">AInora</a>, a vendor of AI phone software.</p>
      <p class="footnote" id="fn7">7. Vendor-reported missed-call reduction after switching to AI answering: <a href="https://calljolt.com/blog/hvac/home-service-industry-phone-statistics" rel="nofollow noopener">CallJolt, 2026</a>. Not independent research, which is why we do not quote it.</p>
      <p class="footnote" id="fn8">8. <a href="https://www.clio.com/blog/highlights-from-2024-legal-trends-report/" rel="nofollow noopener">Clio Legal Trends Report, 2024</a>, secret-shopper study of 500 US law firms, and the onboarding findings in the same report series.</p>
      <p class="footnote" id="fn9">9. 35% of law firm calls unanswered: <a href="https://www.cbs42.com/business/press-releases/ein-presswire/839484491/new-national-study-finds-35-of-law-firm-calls-go-unanswered-costing-industry-an-estimated-109-billion-annually/" rel="nofollow noopener">2025 national industry study</a>, released as a press release.</p>
      <p class="footnote" id="fn10">10. <a href="https://www.callrail.com/blog/missed-calls-cost-businesses-more-than-ever" rel="nofollow noopener">CallRail survey of 1,000 US consumers</a>, 2025, covering businesses in general. CallRail sells call-tracking software.</p>
      <p class="footnote">All figures on this page are projections based on published industry benchmarks and the stated assumptions. They are not guarantees, and individual results vary.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding: 72px 0 24px; }
  .hero h1 { max-width: 22ch; }
  .promise { margin-top: 28px; max-width: 70ch; border-color: var(--amber); }
  .promise p { margin: 0; }
  .total { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px; border-color: var(--amber); }
  .total .stat b { color: var(--amber); font-size: 1.7rem; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .total { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .narrow { max-width: 760px; }
</style>
